## 4. Ranking power

{tbl_ranking}

**Assessment.** Ranking is acceptable for tiering. LightGBM beats the scorecard by {auc_diff_oot:.3f} AUC in 2005 and {auc_diff_cr:.3f} in the crisis; the intervals overlap in 2005 but not in the crisis. In 2016-19 the two are indistinguishable. A gain this small does not justify the explainability and monotonicity cost (Sections 7 and 8). LightGBM also overfits more: its train-to-hold-out AUC gap is {gap_l:.3f}, against {gap_s:.3f} for the scorecard.

